WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.130
DEBI CABRERA: Do you need
to monitor and protect

00:00:02.130 --> 00:00:05.100
large amounts of sensitive
data, but aren't always

00:00:05.100 --> 00:00:07.410
sure where that
data is or how it's

00:00:07.410 --> 00:00:09.300
being processed and managed?

00:00:09.300 --> 00:00:12.750
Today we'll talk about
Automatic DLP, a service

00:00:12.750 --> 00:00:14.850
from Google Cloud that
is built to minimize

00:00:14.850 --> 00:00:18.510
the risk of sensitive data
being mishandled or exposed

00:00:18.510 --> 00:00:21.310
and help you prevent
privacy, security,

00:00:21.310 --> 00:00:22.980
and compliance issues.

00:00:22.980 --> 00:00:26.310
Before we continue, if you need
a refresher on what data loss

00:00:26.310 --> 00:00:28.170
prevention is,
check out the link

00:00:28.170 --> 00:00:31.020
in the description for our
Getting Started with Data Loss

00:00:31.020 --> 00:00:33.320
Prevention playlist.

00:00:33.320 --> 00:00:36.920
First, let's understand
how DLP Inspection works.

00:00:36.920 --> 00:00:41.060
The Cloud DLP Engine inspects
structured and unstructured

00:00:41.060 --> 00:00:44.750
data and classifies it using
what we call info types,

00:00:44.750 --> 00:00:47.210
our predefined data tags.

00:00:47.210 --> 00:00:51.690
Out of the box, DLP provides
over 150 different info types,

00:00:51.690 --> 00:00:54.590
including personally
identifiable information,

00:00:54.590 --> 00:00:58.610
financial data types, global
and region-specific types,

00:00:58.610 --> 00:00:59.570
and more.

00:00:59.570 --> 00:01:03.050
And you can extend these with
custom info types and detection

00:01:03.050 --> 00:01:05.820
rules to meet your
business's needs.

00:01:05.820 --> 00:01:08.180
For example, the DLP
Engine can tell you

00:01:08.180 --> 00:01:10.850
where it found an instance
of a credit card number,

00:01:10.850 --> 00:01:13.070
even giving you details
down to the byte

00:01:13.070 --> 00:01:15.320
offset where it was found.

00:01:15.320 --> 00:01:17.420
For BigQuery, an
inspection job can

00:01:17.420 --> 00:01:20.810
be configured to scan an
individual table in a data set.

00:01:20.810 --> 00:01:22.880
This will leverage
the DLP Engine

00:01:22.880 --> 00:01:25.340
to perform a deep
scan of that table

00:01:25.340 --> 00:01:28.280
to look for sensitive
data elements.

00:01:28.280 --> 00:01:30.500
Info type classification
can be used

00:01:30.500 --> 00:01:33.800
to make informed decisions
about how you protect, share,

00:01:33.800 --> 00:01:35.390
and use your data.

00:01:35.390 --> 00:01:37.730
The DLP Engine and
inspection jobs

00:01:37.730 --> 00:01:40.100
are great at deep
scanning data to get

00:01:40.100 --> 00:01:42.440
very detailed information.

00:01:42.440 --> 00:01:44.810
But when it comes to
gaining visibility

00:01:44.810 --> 00:01:48.770
across your entire organization,
across thousands of projects

00:01:48.770 --> 00:01:50.960
filled with data
sets and tables,

00:01:50.960 --> 00:01:54.050
this scale can become
unmanageable pretty quickly.

00:01:54.050 --> 00:01:57.140
And writing up some custom
code to scan every table

00:01:57.140 --> 00:02:00.360
can lead to a lot of
overhead to manage.

00:02:00.360 --> 00:02:04.760
So we made DLP automatic and
developed a fully-managed data

00:02:04.760 --> 00:02:08.180
profiling service that takes
away that overhead and pain.

00:02:08.180 --> 00:02:11.300
It gives you the same
detection quality as DLP

00:02:11.300 --> 00:02:13.610
and lets you protect
data by identifying

00:02:13.610 --> 00:02:17.840
where sensitive and high-risk
data resides automatically.

00:02:17.840 --> 00:02:22.100
It generates a set of metrics
and insights or a data profile

00:02:22.100 --> 00:02:23.750
from scanning the data.

00:02:23.750 --> 00:02:26.390
Among these metrics are
the protected info types

00:02:26.390 --> 00:02:30.260
found in BigQuery tables,
free text score, and data risk

00:02:30.260 --> 00:02:30.960
level.

00:02:30.960 --> 00:02:35.000
So you gain crucial insights
into what kind of at-risk data

00:02:35.000 --> 00:02:36.950
you are currently
storing, allowing

00:02:36.950 --> 00:02:39.620
you to take the appropriate
steps to protect it.

00:02:39.620 --> 00:02:42.440
Automatic DLP profiler
scans are set up

00:02:42.440 --> 00:02:44.120
with a simple configuration.

00:02:44.120 --> 00:02:47.330
And we'll scan all BigQuery
data sets and tables

00:02:47.330 --> 00:02:51.680
in an entire organization,
folder, or project.

00:02:51.680 --> 00:02:55.520
You may be thinking, these wide
scanning capabilities sound

00:02:55.520 --> 00:02:56.100
great.

00:02:56.100 --> 00:02:59.280
But what if I want to keep
that detailed view of my data?

00:02:59.280 --> 00:03:02.330
Well, you're in luck because
this automatic service

00:03:02.330 --> 00:03:04.940
was built to fit perfectly
with the previous DLP

00:03:04.940 --> 00:03:08.460
functionality, those inspection
jobs we talked about earlier.

00:03:08.460 --> 00:03:10.910
So you can get a
view a mile wide,

00:03:10.910 --> 00:03:14.480
and when needed, a mile deep
when using these together.

00:03:14.480 --> 00:03:17.270
And the fact that automatic
DLP is fully managed

00:03:17.270 --> 00:03:19.550
allows Google Cloud to
take on the overhead

00:03:19.550 --> 00:03:23.280
and allows you to focus on the
outcomes and your business.

00:03:23.280 --> 00:03:25.400
But wait, there's more.

00:03:25.400 --> 00:03:27.830
Continuous monitoring
automatically

00:03:27.830 --> 00:03:30.800
profiles any new tables
you create across your org

00:03:30.800 --> 00:03:34.580
and periodically re-profiles
the tables you modify.

00:03:34.580 --> 00:03:38.120
Data profiles are generated in
the same geographical region

00:03:38.120 --> 00:03:40.400
that your data lives in,
making sure to maintain

00:03:40.400 --> 00:03:41.990
your data residency.

00:03:41.990 --> 00:03:44.750
And deep technical knowledge
of coding or embedding

00:03:44.750 --> 00:03:46.970
isn't necessary to
use the service.

00:03:46.970 --> 00:03:49.580
You focus on configuring
it to your needs,

00:03:49.580 --> 00:03:52.760
turning it on with one click,
and consuming the results.

00:03:52.760 --> 00:03:55.460
And you get all of this
with low overhead, which

00:03:55.460 --> 00:03:58.610
means you don't need to manage
or orchestrate your own jobs.

00:03:58.610 --> 00:04:02.580
So scanning across
your org is a breeze.

00:04:02.580 --> 00:04:04.460
As a quick example,
let's say you

00:04:04.460 --> 00:04:08.120
have 150,000 tables
across multiple projects

00:04:08.120 --> 00:04:10.160
that you need to scan
for sensitive data,

00:04:10.160 --> 00:04:14.270
like Social Security
numbers and email addresses.

00:04:14.270 --> 00:04:16.850
When you turn on
automatic DLP, you'll

00:04:16.850 --> 00:04:19.970
see detailed metrics about
each table and column

00:04:19.970 --> 00:04:23.360
in your organization so that
you can assess your overall data

00:04:23.360 --> 00:04:27.740
risk and gain insights on where
you have that sensitive data.

00:04:27.740 --> 00:04:30.920
Executives who worry about
maintaining security and data

00:04:30.920 --> 00:04:34.190
compliance can see at a high
level where risks may lie.

00:04:34.190 --> 00:04:37.430
And data admins who are
responsible for that data

00:04:37.430 --> 00:04:40.190
can ensure all data is
properly permissioned

00:04:40.190 --> 00:04:42.410
or consider they're
identifying the data

00:04:42.410 --> 00:04:45.200
to protect it and
improve compliance.

00:04:45.200 --> 00:04:47.570
All that were just
a few configuration

00:04:47.570 --> 00:04:50.330
steps and the click of
a button to turn it on--

00:04:50.330 --> 00:04:51.860
easy peasy.

00:04:51.860 --> 00:04:53.660
So let's recap.

00:04:53.660 --> 00:04:57.980
Automatic DLP will help find
sensitive data, including

00:04:57.980 --> 00:05:01.550
unexpected places, keep
up with data growth that

00:05:01.550 --> 00:05:04.160
makes it difficult to
manually inspect data,

00:05:04.160 --> 00:05:08.690
and provide rich insights
about data and data risk,

00:05:08.690 --> 00:05:11.030
allowing you to
manage data risk,

00:05:11.030 --> 00:05:14.610
make more informed decisions,
focus on the outcome,

00:05:14.610 --> 00:05:17.840
and ultimately, help to safely
accelerate your business

00:05:17.840 --> 00:05:20.330
while we take care of the rest.

00:05:20.330 --> 00:05:22.390
Thanks for watching.

